WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.910
This is Jesus. In a moment,

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:05.710
a crowd will choose
a murderer over Him.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:07.310
And that murderer's name…

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.360
will shock you.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.280
Every Passover, the governor
set one prisoner free.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.290
Pilate brought out two men.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.070
Jesus… who healed the
sick and raised the dead.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:24.440
And Barabbas. A rebel who had
"committed murder in the insurrection."

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:29.540
Pilate asked: "Whether of the twain
will ye that I release unto you?"

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.530
And the crowd shouted: "Barabbas."

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.510
But notice his name. In Aramaic,

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.760
"Bar" means son. "Abba" means father.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:43.500
Barabbas means "son of the father."

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.450
So that day, a guilty son
of the father walked free…

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.160
…and the true Son of the
Father died in his place.

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.360
"Then released he Barabbas unto them."

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.240
Barabbas didn't earn it.
He didn't even ask for it.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.950
He walked out… because
Jesus walked in.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.630
"For Christ also hath
once suffered for sins,

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.990
the just for the unjust, that
he might bring us to God."

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:16.490
And here's the truth: you
are Barabbas. So am I.

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:21.220
If you were Barabbas, what would
you say to Jesus? One line.
